# Copy to lab.env and set what differs on your machine; everything else keeps its default from
# defaults.env (lib.sh reads lab.env first, then fills the gaps from defaults.env). All settings, with
# their defaults and which script reads them: docs/settings.md. Nothing in here is secret: the token
# and passwords live in their own files (HA_TOKEN_FILE, TEST_USER_PASSWORD_FILE), never printed.

# Your Home Assistant, as seen from this machine and from the emulator (10.0.2.2 = this machine).
#HA_URL=http://localhost:8123
#HA_URL_EMULATOR=http://10.0.2.2:8123
#HA_TOKEN_FILE=$HOME/.config/ha-companion-lab/ha-token

# Where results, card builds and the lab's data go.
#OUT_DIR=$HOME/ha-companion-lab-data/out
#BUILDS_DIR=$HOME/ha-companion-lab-data/builds

# A node_modules with playwright-core 1.62 for the Playwright scripts (tools/pwa.sh); `lab doctor`
# says how to get one if it is missing.
#PW_NODE_MODULES=$HOME/ha-companion-lab-data/node_modules

# The Avent add-on of the lab's Home Assistant: an aventproxy checkout to copy the integration from.
#AVENT_INTEGRATION_SRC=$HOME/aventproxy
